message.content:
**Proposed change set (protocol‑first, minimal, safe)**  

| File | Change | Why |
|------|--------|-----|
| `apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/metrics.ts` | Add `public getMetrics(): RuntimeMetrics` that returns a **copy** of the internal metrics. | Exposes the server‑side metrics through a read‑only method that the protocol can safely serialize. |
| `apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/types.ts` | Add a new `type RuntimeMetricsEvent = { ts: number; metrics: RuntimeMetrics }` and a new `ServerMessage` case `type: "runtime.metrics"` with payload `{ metrics: RuntimeMetrics }`. | Extends the protocol with a dedicated message type for metrics, keeping the contract explicit and versioned. |
| `apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/GameRuntimeServer.ts` | In `sendSessionState()` (or a new `sendMetrics()` helper) emit a `runtime.metrics` message that contains `this.metrics.snapshot()` and the current timestamp. | Sends the metrics to every connected client as soon as they are available, without breaking existing flows. |
| `apps/game-runtime/test/ui-contract.integration.test.ts` | Add a test that verifies the new `runtime.metrics` message can be parsed and contains the expected fields. | Guarantees the contract is respected and protects against regressions. |

---

### 1. `apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/metrics.ts`

```diff
@@
 export type RuntimeMetrics = {
   turnsTotal: number;
   invalidOutputCount: number;
   actionAppliedCount: number;
   actionRejectedCount: number;
   queuedActions: number;
 };

 export class MetricsTracker {
   ...
+  /** Return a shallow copy – callers cannot mutate internal state. */
+  public getMetrics(): RuntimeMetrics {
+    return { ...this.metrics };
+  }
```

*No other file needs to be edited for this change.*

---

### 2. `apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/types.ts`

```diff
@@
 export type RuntimeMetrics = {
   turnsTotal: number;
   invalidOutputCount: number;
   actionAppliedCount: number;
   actionRejectedCount: number;
   queuedActions: number;
 };

+/** A single snapshot of runtime metrics together with a timestamp. */
+export type RuntimeMetricsEvent = {
+  /** Unix epoch ms when the snapshot was taken. */
+  ts: number;
+  /** Metrics values. */
+  metrics: RuntimeMetrics;
+};
+
+/** All messages that can be sent from the server to the client. */
+export type ServerMessage =
+  | {
+      version: Version;
+      type: "session.state";
+      payload: {
+        phase: SessionPhase;
+        paused: boolean;
+        preparedSeed: number | null;
+        threadIds: { gameplayByAgentId: Record<string, string>; builder?: string };
+        connected: boolean;
+        runtime: {
+          model: string | null;
+          effort: TurnEffort;
+          tickMs: number;
+          schedulerMs: number;
+          maxQueuedActionsBeforeTurn: number;
+          availableModels: RuntimeModelOption[];
+        };
+      };
+    }
+  | {
+      version: Version;
+      type: "world.snapshot";
+      payload: { /* unchanged */ }
+    }
+  | {
+      version: Version;
+      type: "agent.turn";
+      payload: { /* unchanged */ }
+    }
+  | {
+      version: Version;
+      type: "agent.action";
+      payload: { /* unchanged */ }
+    }
+  | {
+      version: Version;
+      type: "agent.feed";
+      payload: { /* unchanged */ }
+    }
+  | {
+      version: Version;
+      type: "build.result";
+      payload: { /* unchanged */ }
+    }
+  | {
+      version: Version;
+      type: "error";
+      payload: { /* unchanged */ }
+    }
+  /** Metrics snapshot sent to the client. */
+  | {
+      version: Version;
+      type: "runtime.metrics";
+      payload: {
+        ts: number;
+        metrics: RuntimeMetrics;
+      };
+    };
```

*Only the new `runtime.metrics` case is added; all existing cases stay untouched.*

---

